{"type":"text","timestamp":1794230296272,"sessionID":"ses_e3f8db8beffeL0ILaBUom45yfp","part":{"id":"prt_1c0758013001L57pySFsMA7Bmz","sessionID":"ses_e3f8db8beffeL0ILaBUom45yfp","messageID":"msg_1c072bf330013ZEt6ZVmEAEnOI","type":"text","text":"Here's an example of how to use the `opencode.models` tool to search for available models:\n\n```javascript\nasync function listAvailableModels() {\n  try {\n    const result = await tools.opencode.models({\n      query: \"gpt\",\n      type: \"chat\",\n      limit: 5\n    });\n    \n    console.log(\"Available models:\");\n    result.providers.forEach(provider => {\n      console.log(`Provider: ${provider.name}`);\n      provider.models.forEach(model => {\n        console.log(`- ${model.name} (ID: ${model.id})`);\n      });\n    });\n  } catch (error) {\n    console.error(\"Error fetching models:\", error);\n  }\n}\n```\n\nKey points:\n1. Use `await` to handle the promise\n2. Pass parameters as an object (not as separate arguments)\n3. Handle the response structure appropriately\n4. Error handling is recommended\n\nFor MCP resource discovery:\n```javascript\nasync function discoverMcpResources() {\n  try {\n    const resources = await tools.opencode.list_mcp_resources();\n    console.log(\"Discovered MCP resources:\", resources);\n  } catch (error) {\n    console.error(\"MCP resource discovery failed:\", error);\n  }\n}\n```\n\nRemember to always handle errors and validate parameters when using these tools. The tools are designed to be used with `await` rather than as keys in an object.","time":{"start":1794230288403,"end":1794230296272}}}
